{
  "id": "ep152",
  "duration": 51.336,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.082,
      "text": "Shine so brightly that astronomers study it in broad daylight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C-west-1976-ps.jpg",
        "credit": "J. Linder/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C-west-1976-ps.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.082,
      "end": 11.727,
      "text": "On August tenth, 1975, astronomer Richard M. West discovered the icy visitor plunging toward the Sun.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The ESO 1-metre Schmidt telescope (lasilla-construction).jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/F. Middelburg",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_ESO_1-metre_Schmidt_telescope_(lasilla-construction).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.067,
          "end": 7.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.633,
          "end": 11.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.727,
      "end": 19.922,
      "text": "In February 1976, the comet reached perihelion, racing within thirty million kilometers of the solar surface.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.733,
          "end": 19.933,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.922,
      "end": 26.942,
      "text": "Solar heat and forward scattering pushed its brightness to magnitude minus three, making it as bright as Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C-west-mar1976-ps.jpg",
        "credit": "P. St\u00e4ttmayer/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C-west-mar1976-ps.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.933,
          "end": 23.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 23.833,
          "end": 26.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.942,
      "end": 33.387,
      "text": "From February twenty-fifth to the twenty-seventh, observers tracked the dazzling object in the middle of the day.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Comet West 1975n.jpg",
        "credit": "coniferconifer",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comet_West_1975n.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.933,
          "end": 33.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.387,
      "end": 40.057,
      "text": "But the sun's gravity was a hammer, shattering the comet's nucleus into four distinct, glowing fragments.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hubble Provides Spectacular Detail of a Comet's Breakup (2006-18-1902).jpg",
        "credit": "Hubble Images (top): , , H. Weaver (JHU/APL), M. Mutchler and Z. Levay (); Ground-Based Image (bottom): G. Rhemann and M. Jager",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubble_Provides_Spectacular_Detail_of_a_Comet%27s_Breakup_(2006-18-1902).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.4,
          "end": 37.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 37.467,
          "end": 40.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.057,
      "end": 46.902,
      "text": "This broken traveler will now spend hundreds of thousands of years drifting through the darkness of deep space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rubin Oort Cloud and Kuiper Belt Illustration (rubin-Oort-Cloud-and-Kuiper-Belt).tiff",
        "credit": "RubinObs/NOIRLab/SLAC/NSF/DOE/AURA",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubin_Oort_Cloud_and_Kuiper_Belt_Illustration_(rubin-Oort-Cloud-and-Kuiper-Belt).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.067,
          "end": 46.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 46.902,
      "end": 50.986,
      "text": "This unprecedented display proves that a single comet can",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C-west-1976-ps.jpg",
        "credit": "J. Linder/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C-west-1976-ps.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 46.9,
          "end": 51.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
